# Verify before you reply (owner 2026-11-11)

The owner should never find a difference you did not. "Looks fine" is not a check. Before you say a UI change is
done, do all of this, and say in the reply what you checked and what you did not:

1. **Compare like with like across the whole office, not only the page you touched.** For each kind of element you
   changed or saw — the page's main button, other head buttons, ⋯ menus, tabs, filters, tables (header, row height,
   sort), badges, empty states, dialogs (head, body, foot), fact rows, cards, toasts — list every page that has one and
   compare them: same component, same variant, same size, same colour, same place. The reference is the element the
   owner named or the one in `DESIGN.md`, never "they match each other".
2. **Measure, then look.** Read the computed styles (height, colours, border, radius, font) of the same element on
   every page with a script against the running copy (port 3000), then look at full-size screenshots, not thumbnails.
3. **Every width and theme:** 390, 768, 1280 at least; ar-dark and en-light at least; he when copy changed. Re-run
   `apps/web/visual-audit/` (see `docs/reviews/2026-11-11-visual-audit.md`) and read its findings.
4. **Interact, don't only render.** Click what you changed: switches, sort headers, tabs, dialogs, saves. Watch that
   nothing on the page jumps (measure the table's top before and after), that messages do not push content, and that
   the state after the action is right.
5. **Every state:** empty, loading, error, one row, many rows, long names, unlimited/none values.
6. **Report honestly:** what was checked, at which widths and themes, what was found and fixed, and anything not
   checked. Never write "all consistent" unless step 1 was done for that element on every page.
